.Dd September 19, 2026
.Dt DHCPC 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dhcpc
.Nd acquire and maintain a DHCP lease
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl i Ar INTERFACE
.Op Fl b
.Op Fl l Ar SECONDS
.Nm
.Op Fl i Ar INTERFACE
.Fl k
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the DHCP client for images without BusyBox.
It validates the lease before applying the address, netmask, default route,
and resolver configuration.
A missing netmask selects the address's classful mask for both validation
and application, including renewals of an unchanged address.
A packet socket receives replies before the interface has an address.
Each resolver update writes and closes a private temporary file before
renaming it over
.Pa /etc/resolv.conf .
Concurrent writers publish complete versions; the last rename selects
the current version.
A lease with no DNS servers still replaces the file.
.Pp
The client maintains the lease for as long as it runs.
It renews at T1, the renewal time, and rebinds at T2, the rebinding time:
the server's values when it gives valid ones, otherwise one half and seven
eighths of the lease.
At expiry or on DHCPNAK, it removes the address and starts discovery again.
If removal fails, it exits with the recorded address and claim retained
for a later client or
.Fl k
to retry cleanup.
Leases shorter than 10 seconds are ignored.
Leases longer than one week, or the limit selected with
.Fl l ,
are capped.
There is no configure-once mode.
.Pp
Only one client may configure an interface at a time.
The client creates
.Pa /var/run/dhcpc.INTERFACE.pid
with
.Dv O_EXCL
and records its process ID and configured address there.
The file is visible before the process ID is written.
An empty or unreadable claim is treated as busy.
It does not use
.Xr fcntl 2
locks.
.Pp
On os-real, BusyBox's
.Ic udhcpc
performs this job through the same kernel interface; see
.Xr busybox-networking 1 .
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl i Ar INTERFACE
Use this interface.
The default is
.Ql eth0 .
.It Fl b
Enter the background after the first discovery round, which makes up to
four requests, whether or not the interface was configured.
The child closes inherited standard descriptors and redirects them to the
console, or to
.Pa /dev/null
if the console cannot be opened.
If redirection fails, the child exits with its claim retained for cleanup.
.It Fl l Ar SECONDS
Limit the lease to this many seconds.
The accepted range is 10 through 604800.
.It Fl k
Stop the client recorded for the interface.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /var/run/dhcpc.INTERFACE.pid
The interface's client process ID and configured address.
.It Pa /etc/resolv.conf
Resolver configuration written from the lease.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Acquire and maintain a lease on eth0, entering the background after
the first discovery round:
.Dl dhcpc -b
.Ql tests/run dhcp
exercises lease acquisition, renewal, and the address's removal with
.Fl k .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr busybox-networking 1 ,
.Xr netup 8
